  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `{cite}` of `requirements.authoring.usage_storage` on `src/authoring/usage.rs#struct[UsageLog]` is appropriate.\n\n- **Not a test.** `UsageLog` is a plain struct, so `{test}` does not apply.\n- **No `{impl}` needed.** `UsageLog` makes no decisions and does no checks. The serialized form lives in `src/authoring/usage.rs#struct[UsageRecord]`. The storage path and file writing live in `src/authoring/usage.rs#impl[UsageLog]/fn[start]` and `fn[save]`. The requirement's behavior is already implemented by marked items in `src/authoring/mod.rs`: `fn[author_evidence_with_output]`, `fn[backend_name]`, `fn[prepare_assessment]`, `impl[PendingAssessment]/fn[failed]` and `impl[PendingAssessment]/fn[persisted]`. Those items use `UsageLog`, so it is reached from them and needs no `{impl}` of its own.\n- **`{cite}` fits.** The struct holds the per-assessment record and the path of its JSON file under `<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json`. It exists to give each assessment a separate persisted usage record. A change to what the requirement says a record or its storage must contain could require changing this struct.\n- **No redundancy.** The item has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same requirement, so the citation is not redundant.",
  "inputs": [
